@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title G4 · Follow one destruction or release obligation
hide footbox
$caller(caller, "Caller")
$callee(callee, "Callee")
== Borrowed input ==
note over caller : Before entry: caller holds one obligation.
caller --> callee : At entry: lend access to the handle
note over caller, callee
  After entry: caller still holds the obligation.
  Borrowing transfers none to the callee.
end note
== Consumed input ==
note over caller : Before entry: caller holds one obligation.
caller -> callee : At entry: transfer the handle's obligation
note over callee : Just after entry: callee holds the obligation.
note over caller, callee
  Success or failure does not undo this transfer.
  The callee discharges the obligation unless it
  explicitly returns it as an owned output.
end note
== Non-null owned result ==
note over callee : Before delivery: callee holds the obligation to give.
callee -> caller : At delivery: give the handle and one obligation
note over caller : After delivery: caller holds one obligation.
note over caller, callee
  A null result supplies no obligation.
  Separate strong retention creates another obligation;
  it does not transfer the caller's existing one.
end note
legend bottom
  Three separate cases, not one call sequence. Time runs downward within each case.
  Actor = caller; rectangular participant = callee.
  Solid arrow = ownership transfer; dashed arrow = borrowed access.
  Notes track the obligation, not exclusive access or pointer copies.
  Non-normative: C2, C3, C5. No retention event is drawn.
endlegend
@enduml
